FAQ
FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS

WHO IS FRAMOUS?

Stage name for RYAN LEE PRESSON. For any number of reasons, I decided to use an alternative that would help to identify myself as someone searching for more than being just another artist on the wall. The Frame became a creative boundary for working and thinking about what to create next. The mutated core idea is just being able to make a living at it and not really seeking fame or crooked frames.     

WANT TO KNOW MORE ABOUT vGallerySpace?

The name is intentionally generic and uses a case-sensitive URL because most people are hypersensitive these days. There have been many iterations, starting as a portfolio site and growing into online exhibitions, with the GALLERY being the storefront or facade. The shopping carts host a number of places that I collect, buy, and sell artwork of those who influence the marketplace and my own work.

Built using OpenClaw, Gemini, and Hermes Agentic AI on top of the Bootstrap 5 framework, HTML5, JavaScript, and more.  

WHAT IS STUDIO?

A place for experimentation, mainly documenting the work for arch>scul and other artworks. Most of my time is spent reviewing my concepts, researching the work of others, and strategizing about the market or new areas of discipline. A few projects get selected and developed further for exhibition while the rest get filtered through the OFFICE for review. 

TELL ME ABOUT arch>scul?
		
Originally conceived from a painting made in the late 1990s, then some architects, and wood cut down to make a chess board. While sitting in the corner, the blocks became a solution of the 1+1=3 equation modified with a "many more" approach. The prototypes are essentially models used to test the belief that architecture is just as great as sculpture. The goal is to one day actually build the sculptures into a full-blown building.

WHERE IS GALLERY?

The location is virtual, always online for visitors to roam. Occasionally, some of the work makes it into a group show or brick-and-mortar gallery for viewing, with both STUDIO and OFFICE extensions complementing each other with variations of GSO/GOS + SGO/SOG or OSG/OGS—continuously learning parts to make a better whole.

WHY DO YOU CALL YOURSELF A STRATEGIC ARTIST?

My background is in Marketing, Advertising & Promotions, but I have always been an artist more or less at pivotal points in time. I was particularly interested in taking these same skills I have learned and merging them all together to form new kinds of artworks.  

HOW DID YOU MAKE THE AI DOCENT?

Initially named via ChatGPT, she became the subject and docent for the Infinity Museum—the artificial muse concept, evolving into the AI Docent RESA.

NEED HELP WITH STRATEGY OR TO PRODUCE WORK WITH THE OFFICE?

I am currently collaborating with Agentic AI now and can produce all types of media. I have in the past helped a variety of businesses with building their presence.  
